---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/blog-placeholder-about.jpg';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Pattern-spotting the AI-tool ecosystem."
	pubDate={new Date('July 28 2026')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<p>
		Shift Spotters is a pattern-spotter and trend-cartographer for the AI-tool
		ecosystem. It watches what's happening in AI dev tools, agent frameworks,
		coding CLIs, and the surrounding infrastructure — and writes about what's
		actually changing versus what's just noise.
	</p>

	<p>
		The audience is developers primarily, and business/creator readers who want
		to understand where AI tooling is heading without wading through vendor
		marketing. Same articles serve both — most content is technical enough for
		engineers and framed clearly enough for non-engineers who need to make
		decisions about which tools their teams are betting on.
	</p>

	<h2>What to expect</h2>
	<p>
		Category tours, pattern analysis, and honest reads on where specific tools
		sit in the ecosystem. The lens is <em>informative, not adversarial</em> — no
		roasting, no vendor bashing. Honest critique of products and companies is
		fair game. Personal attacks on creators or channels are not.
	</p>

	<p>
		Content is substance-first. Graphics support the writing, not the other way
		around. If a piece would be shorter and clearer at 1,200 words instead of
		1,800, it stays at 1,200.
	</p>

	<h2>How this site is made</h2>
	<p>
		<em>This channel combines original research with AI-assisted writing and production.</em>
	</p>

	<p>
		Data collection and pattern-analysis happens through a purpose-built
		pipeline. Article drafting is AI-assisted with human review at every stage.
		Never used: AI-generated depictions of real people, synthetic events, or
		deepfakes.
	</p>

	<h2>Sponsors</h2>
	<p>
		None, currently. Shift Spotters is not being paid by any of the tools,
		companies, or platforms it covers. If that changes, we'll say so — clearly,
		in this section and in any piece where it's relevant.
	</p>

	<h2>Factchecking and updates</h2>
	<p>
		Every article on this site includes a "last factchecked" date alongside
		its publication date. Articles get revised as tools and dynamics shift —
		the last-factchecked date updates whenever a piece is re-verified against
		current reality.
	</p>

	<p>
		Our factchecking methods are not perfect. If something in an article looks
		factually incorrect, we're open to revising it. Email
		<a href="mailto:hello@shiftspotters.com">hello@shiftspotters.com</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Reach out at <a href="mailto:hello@shiftspotters.com">hello@shiftspotters.com</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
